WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the twentieth of August. Have we got everyone on Teams?</v>

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.199
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'm here. Only just, mind. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid.</v>

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:15.519
<v David Whitfield>Same queue, different Thursday.</v>

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:23.940
<v Grace Liu>I'm hoping it clears up for the weekend. Meant to be going camping, but that weather forecast's looking properly grim.</v>

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.129
<v Marcus Hale>Camping? In this? Brave.</v>

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:30.760
<v Grace Liu>That's one word for it. Anyway, yes, I'm here.</v>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Quick bit on what's already finished, then the actual jobs.</v>

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.850
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, I signed off the inspection on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve on Tuesday.</v>

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:48.219
<v David Whitfield>That's fully closed, then? Not something hanging over from Tuesday?</v>

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:53.130
<v Aisha Begum>Fully closed. Just reporting it, nothing new there.</v>

00:00:55.429 --> 00:01:01.729
<v Sarah Okafor>And I signed off the inspection on the Site Water System on Tuesday. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:11.599
<v Sarah Okafor>One observation from me: saw the pressure on the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.780
<v Priya Raman>It recovered without anyone changing anything?</v>

00:01:16.189 --> 00:01:20.739
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah. Just an observation for this meeting, not allocating a job off that.</v>

00:01:21.769 --> 00:01:30.170
<v Marcus Hale>Similar sort of thing here. I saw the pressure on the relief valve dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own.</v>

00:01:32.099 --> 00:01:34.549
<v Aisha Begum>You're just reporting what you saw, yeah?</v>

00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:38.670
<v Marcus Hale>Exactly. Not proposing any work on it.</v>

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:46.129
<v Priya Raman>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the water booster. Still blocked, I'm afraid.</v>

00:01:46.709 --> 00:01:50.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that stays blocked. No new chasing action out of this meeting.</v>

00:01:52.930 --> 00:02:00.980
<v David Whitfield>Oh, and we were going to replace the belt on the line one but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.680
<v Callum Reid>Good, because that's still on the old printout. Definitely not today's work?</v>

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.810
<v David Whitfield>Definitely not. Pushed to next month.</v>

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:17.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus Hale, can you run the monthly fire alarm test next week? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:02:18.969 --> 00:02:23.169
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test next week. Got it.</v>

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.349
<v Grace Liu>Amazing how that sound still makes everyone jump, even when they're expecting it.</v>

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:36.000
<v Sarah Okafor>And Marc, can you send the shift handover report round tomorrow? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.300
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow.</v>

00:02:42.009 --> 00:02:45.860
<v Callum Reid>That's the existing handover report, isn't it? Not a different version?</v>

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.939
<v Marcus Hale>Just the existing one, yeah. Nothing fancy.</v>

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:58.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, can you also do a site visit at Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor next week? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:58.509 --> 00:03:05.159
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I can do that. I'll do the site visit at Kestrel in Leeds with the contractor next week.</v>

00:03:06.939 --> 00:03:12.889
<v David Whitfield>Full name, short name, middle-sized name. Thought we'd got three operators on the call for a second.</v>

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.509
<v Marcus Hale>Unfortunately it's just me, mate.</v>

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:24.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you inspect the PRV on the boiler for leaks next week? Again, not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:25.949 --> 00:03:32.949
<v Aisha Begum>Yep—sorry, just separating that from my completed inspection update. This is the leak inspection on the PRV on the boiler?</v>

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:38.659
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. Separate job, next week, not reopening Tuesday's sign-off.</v>

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:44.319
<v Aisha Begum>Understood. I'll inspect the PRV on the boiler for leaks next week.</v>

00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:51.409
<v Grace Liu>Um, I'll grease and check the bearings on the number two bearing today at 2pm. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:56.199
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, you clipped a bit there. Number two bearing?</v>

00:03:57.219 --> 00:04:01.419
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, the number two bearing. Grease and check the bearings on that.</v>

00:04:02.729 --> 00:04:06.229
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Grace Liu has that, today at 2pm, low priority.</v>

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.509
<v Grace Liu>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:19.910
<v Callum Reid>Then there's the chiller on three. We need someone to run a function test on the chiller on three at half two. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:21.829 --> 00:04:27.079
<v Priya Raman>I can't take that one. Just saying now, rather than it looking like I've agreed.</v>

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.439
<v David Whitfield>Nor can I, sorry.</v>

00:04:31.899 --> 00:04:36.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take the function test? We haven't got an owner from that.</v>

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.509
<v Marcus Hale>No, sorry. I can't commit to that one either.</v>

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, nobody's taken it. It's still needed, and it's still safety critical. Not agreed to anyone.</v>

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.029
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, Callum, I talked over the time. Was that half two?</v>

00:04:54.079 --> 00:05:00.730
<v Callum Reid>Half two, yes. And the urgency was straight away, safety critical. I'm raising it, not volunteering to do it.</v>

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:04.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Leaving that explicitly unallocated, not marking it covered.</v>

00:05:05.699 --> 00:05:12.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Callum, can you sort the training records for the new starters tomorrow, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:17.980
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters tomorrow. That's fine.</v>

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.620
<v Grace Liu>Just the records, not another round of training sessions?</v>

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.550
<v Callum Reid>Just sorting the records. No new sessions.</v>

00:05:27.209 --> 00:05:34.209
<v Sarah Okafor>So tomorrow's agreed bits are the shift handover report round from Marc and the new starter training records from Callum.</v>

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.199
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, report's mine.</v>

00:05:38.449 --> 00:05:40.199
<v Callum Reid>And records are mine, yeah.</v>

00:05:41.329 --> 00:05:44.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Any corrections to what's agreed, before we finish?</v>

00:05:45.829 --> 00:05:51.430
<v Priya Raman>No. Just to be clear, water booster is still blocked, not quietly back on the list.</v>

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.230
<v David Whitfield>And the belt replacement's still off. Nothing else from me.</v>

00:05:55.899 --> 00:06:01.500
<v Grace Liu>All good. Apart from the prospect of a wet tent, but that's not for this meeting.</v>

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:05.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Definitely outside our scope. Right, thanks everyone.</v>

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.370
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers. Bye.</v>
